// A `use` binds in the file that writes it. This directory has no manifest, so neither file derives
// a module path and neither declares a `namespace` — helper.noe is a script that happens to sit
// next door, not a module of this program. Its `use std.io` must therefore leave `io` unbound here.
//
// The linker admits a pooled file as an import **driver** on the same condition it admits it as a
// resolution candidate: it declares a namespace. Without that filter a namespace-less neighbour got
// no alias table, so its retained `use std.io` kept the bare name `io` and was prepended to the
// merged program — into the flat top-level scope these statements run in. `noeta check` then
// reported this file clean while `noeta run` refused it.
// expect: error E0005 at 12:1
// expect: exit 1
io.errln("victim")
